# CTT: stable symlink for the Telit LE910Q1 AT control port (USB interface 02):
# /dev/ctt-modem-at.
#
# ModemManager uses interface 02 as the modem's AT port (signal/registration),
# and it floats across /dev/ttyACMx between boots, so we give it a fixed name.
# That fixed name is what ctt-modem-provision binds the ECM data path on: it
# ensures the USB composition is ECM (AT#USBCFG=1) and starts the CDC-ECM session
# (AT#ECM=1,0) at boot — the session, unlike the old RNDIS NV binding, does not
# persist across a modem power-cycle and must be re-issued every boot
# (ctt-modem-provision.service, ordered Before=ModemManager).
#
# CRITICAL: match by VID + interface only, NOT product id. Interface 02 is the AT
# port in BOTH the RNDIS (1bc7:7020) and ECM (1bc7:7021) compositions. A station
# still on RNDIS must expose /dev/ctt-modem-at so ctt-modem-provision can reach
# the modem to switch it to ECM — pinning this to 7021 would make the symlink
# absent on exactly the modems that still need migrating (chicken-and-egg).
# Telit-VID scoped (1bc7) — Quectel/QMI and every other device is untouched.
#
# Match on the tty's own ID_* properties (set by the usb_id builtin in the
# earlier 60-serial rules), NOT ATTRS{}: idVendor/idProduct live on the USB
# device while bInterfaceNumber lives on the interface — different parents, and
# udev requires all ATTRS{} in one rule to match the SAME parent, so an ATTRS
# matcher can never match all three. ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM=="02" selects the AT
# control port (ModemManager's primary AT port).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="1bc7", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", SYMLINK+="ctt-modem-at"
